WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:54.110
Ha-ha! Heso!

3
00:01:54.090 --> 00:02:00.480
<b>The Village Hidden in the Clouds</b>

4
00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:55.940
You boys had better
catch her pretty soon.

5
00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.990
She's getting away.

6
00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.450
He's right, you guys.

7
00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.910
We need to get moving now,
before we lose sight of her.

8
00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.740
Ugh. If we lose her
in this forest,

9
00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.040
finding her again
could be impossible.

10
00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:10.210
Usopp, wait. Finding each
other won't be easy either.

11
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.760
Luffy, you coming?

12
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.810
You two go on ahead without me.

13
00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.070
I'm gonna take care of ball guy.

14
00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.820
Ha-ha! This should be amusing.

15
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.990
Do you really think you can
beat me, rubber boy? Ha-ha!

16
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.450
I guess someone needs to deal

17
00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.160
with this potbellied freak.

18
00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.380
Don't do anything reckless.

19
00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.840
He has weird powers.

20
00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.470
Back as soon as we get the boat!

21
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:32.680
Great.

22
00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:37.510
It's just you and me now, fatso.

23
00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.260
He'll grab that branch.

24
00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.400
And Gum-Gum...

25
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.940
Same move as before.

26
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.400
...Pistol!

27
00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.190
Oh, good.

28
00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.150
Looks like this one will be
sticking around a while.

29
00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.690
Now, where did those
others scamper off to?

30
00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.880
I'll be oh so disappointed
if they got away.

31
00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.540
Hmm. There we are.

32
00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:44.420
Hey! Usopp! You see it yet?

33
00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.500
There she is!

34
00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.630
Wanna tell me where?

35
00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:55.800
Straight ahead!

36
00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.920
Climb up the... one, two...
third tree on the right!

37
00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.380
You can jump on when
she passes beneath you!

38
00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.590
Gotcha!

39
00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:19.620
Aw, crap! It's that priest!

40
00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:20.960
What's he doing?

41
00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:25.520
Heads up, Sanji!

42
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.270
Killer ball, coming your way!

43
00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.020
What? What's Luffy
doing back there?

44
00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.620
Surprise Cloud Billiards!

45
00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.700
Huh?

46
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.010
Usopp!

47
00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.800
That fat freak
was aiming for me!

48
00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.810
At least I
died like a man.

49
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.350
What...? A flower?

50
00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.810
It was a dud.

51
00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.700
Bastard!

52
00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:12.910
All right, you! That does it!

53
00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:13.990
...Now you made me mad!

54
00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.080
– Hm?
– Now you made me mad!

55
00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.200
Gum-Gum...

56
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.790
...Gatling!

57
00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:27.820
Luffy, stop!

58
00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.090
Use your head! You're
only making things worse!

59
00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.300
Huh?

60
00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.180
What the...? What the... ahh!

61
00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:37.840
Oh, no!

62
00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:40.190
It's too late!

63
00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:41.710
Take cover!

64
00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.790
They're coming at us
from all sides!

65
00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.670
Have fun, boys,
I'll be watching!

66
00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.470
Hm? Spears! Crab!

67
00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:05.150
Not four at once!

68
00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:11.940
What the...

69
00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.480
Another dud?

70
00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.870
Nah, I'm not that lucky.

71
00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.580
Hot, hot, hot, hot, hot!

72
00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.310
River! River!

73
00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.620
I went straight through!

74
00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.700
Luffy! You gotta catch yourself!

75
00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:57.660
None of these rivers
have a bottom!

76
00:06:57.740 --> 00:06:59.500
Huh?

77
00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.970
Too much!

78
00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.150
Will you get serious?!

79
00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:30.190
– Usopp Hammer!

80
00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.280
– Rubber band of doom.

81
00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.560
– Yahoo!

82
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.280
Ha, ha! Ya, ha!

83
00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.450
Oh, yeah, that reminds me.

84
00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.620
I should try out my new thingy!

85
00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.960
What's up, Usopp?
You got an idea?

86
00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.630
Do I? Friend, they don't call me

87
00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.930
"Usopp the Technological-
Pirate-Wizard" for nothin'!

88
00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.600
Behold! My latest invention!

89
00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:15.060
"Usopp"...

90
00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:16.380
Yeah... what?

91
00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:18.300
Heh. Just watch!

92
00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.600
Ah. There's the Crow!

93
00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.560
Milky Road, straight ahead!

94
00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.270
Perfect.

95
00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:28.350
Here we go! Line out!

96
00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:40.200
Hm? Now what are they up to?

97
00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:48.500
Yes. Now I just have to swing
over there and catch the Crow!

98
00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.810
But my timing's gotta
be absolutely perfect!

99
00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:52.180
If I miss it, that's it!

100
00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:54.930
We've only got one shot at this!

101
00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.730
Ahh. Not bad.

102
00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.730
But how're you gonna
get past those spheres?

103
00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.570
Just let me worry about that.

104
00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:02.360
Did I happen to mention
they also call me

105
00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.030
"King of the Jungle"? Heh.

106
00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.740
Here goes.

107
00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:12.620
Usopp...!

108
00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.290
Dammit! Just jump!

109
00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.380
Yeah, um... about that.

110
00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.300
Just one small problem.

111
00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.720
I forgot the rope is sort
of attached to the belt.

112
00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.010
I never really got around
to fixing that part.

113
00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.760
Throw me some scissors
or somethin'.

114
00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:44.560
Crap! Crap! Crap! Crap!
Crap! Crap! Crap!

115
00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:50.280
Crap! Crap, crap, crap...

116
00:09:58.330 --> 00:09:59.910
Yoohoo! Hey, Usopp!

117
00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:02.190
What do you think?
This is a lot of fun, isn't it?

118
00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:08.530
I think I need to have a
little word with those two.

119
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.630
Here's the deal.

120
00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:22.920
I'm gonna forget about
what just happened.

121
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.920
But now you do what I say.

122
00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.630
Right. I'm sorry.

123
00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:29.010
Yeah, me, too. What he said.

124
00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:30.420
Okay then.

125
00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.640
First thing, we're gonna
forget about the boat for now.

126
00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:37.060
Then we're gonna all charge
that fat freak at once.

127
00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.110
I don't care what
kinda powers he's got.

128
00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.530
With all three of us
attacking at the same time,

129
00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.480
if there's a way to
beat him, we'll find it.

130
00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.520
Oh? Don't be so sure!

131
00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.800
Where did he go?

132
00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.810
Heh, heh.

133
00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.610
Impact!

134
00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.990
– Sanji!
– Sanji!

135
00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.790
Ha, ha, ha!

136
00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.040
Like they say, "Life is pain."

137
00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.250
Now, who wants to go next?

138
00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:34.920
Hey, uh, did something
just move over there?

139
00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:35.870
I'm not getting attacked
by those sharks again!

140
00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:36.820
This is the One Whistle!

141
00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:37.130
But wait! We still
don't know your name!

142
00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:37.460
Yeah. Where are we
supposed to go from here?

143
00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.660
Fine. Tell you what.

144
00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.130
Just to be safe,
I'll hold on to the whistle.

145
00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.090
Any objections?

146
00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:46.880
What is with you people?

147
00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.630
C'mon, I'm clearly
the weakest one here.

148
00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.030
I need it more than you do!

149
00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:51.200
– But...
– But nothing!

150
00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.070
It's the only thing
that makes sense!

151
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.120
I wanna blow it!

152
00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.700
No! Forget it, Luffy!

153
00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.620
If we give it to you,
you're just gonna waste it!

154
00:11:57.670 --> 00:11:59.010
It's not a toy!

155
00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:01.720
Oh, come on! I wanna call
that weird old guy again!

156
00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:03.020
No. Let me have it!

157
00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.090
I'm the weakest one here,
I should hold it!

158
00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.190
You wish!

159
00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.150
I'm the weakest,
and you all know it!

160
00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:10.230
Oh, please!
How can you say that?

161
00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:12.490
I'm just a poor,
defenseless girl!

162
00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.870
No way! I'm weakest,
and I'm smallest!

163
00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:16.820
Hey! I can be
pretty damn helpless

164
00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:18.200
when I put my mind to it!

165
00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:19.790
No fair! It's not my fault...

166
00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:22.850
Fighting over who's
most pathetic. Odd.

167
00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:28.430
Okay! Here's how
we're gonna do this!

168
00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.610
Center of the ship!

169
00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:31.820
We leave the whistle
on the main mast here,

170
00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:33.320
so if any of us
gets into trouble,

171
00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.410
all we have to do is run
over here and blow it.

172
00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:36.820
Now it's fair to everyone.

173
00:12:36.990 --> 00:12:37.740
Fine.

174
00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:39.290
Okay.

175
00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.790
And, last thing.

176
00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.170
None of you are
allowed to blow it

177
00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:44.130
under any circumstances. Got it?

178
00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:46.800
Aw. Can't I just
call him one time?

179
00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.090
You touch this whistle,

180
00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.760
and you'll be swimming
with the sky fish!

181
00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:52.350
– Fine. We got it.
– Fine. We got it.

182
00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:55.740
Now if anything
really bad happens,

183
00:12:55.820 --> 00:12:58.160
the Sky Knight
will come save me!

184
00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:01.530
But, I can only blow
it as a last resort!

185
00:13:02.620 --> 00:13:03.410
Hear that?

186
00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:04.900
Anyone wants to take this ship,

187
00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:07.230
they have to get
through me first!

188
00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:21.090
What's that?

189
00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:33.680
Just one?

190
00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.470
Surely you're not the only
sacrifice I get to kill?

191
00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:54.500
Huh?

192
00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:57.460
I'm referring to the pumpkins.

193
00:13:57.550 --> 00:14:00.170
I don't think I've ever
grown them quite as sweet.

194
00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:01.260
Hm.

195
00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:05.600
Of course. I'm sorry, but my
mind is wandering elsewhere.

196
00:14:05.680 --> 00:14:07.600
It's very kind of
you to take us in.

197
00:14:07.690 --> 00:14:09.570
I dislike putting you
in this position.

198
00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.070
Not at all.

199
00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.650
If they believe
that your daughter

200
00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:14.330
let the Straw Hats escape,

201
00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:16.190
they'll consider
you an accomplice.

202
00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:18.570
The only safe place
for you is here.

203
00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.410
You can consider this
one on the house.

204
00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:27.600
We're all lucky that Eneru's
Mantra doesn't reach this far.

205
00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.890
How are things
back on the island?

206
00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:35.590
I'm sorry?

207
00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:36.800
The crops.

208
00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:38.800
Are they coming in
hardy this year?

209
00:14:38.880 --> 00:14:41.890
From what I know of it, yes.
Quite well, indeed.

210
00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.930
Well, that's good to hear.

211
00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.720
I prepared us
some pumpkin juice

212
00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:48.520
made from the very ones
that grow here in my field.

213
00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.120
Wonderful flavor.

214
00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.220
Try some.

215
00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.610
Thank you.

216
00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:54.940
It looks refreshing.

217
00:14:55.030 --> 00:14:57.650
Conis, dear.
You should try this.

218
00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.250
Young lady,
I'm curious if you've ever

219
00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:10.960
heard tale of those from the
Blue Sea World called 'pirates.'

220
00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:14.000
Never.

221
00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:15.670
They are basically
just criminals

222
00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:17.760
who travel on the water.

223
00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:20.300
And though each ship
may vary somewhat,

224
00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:23.090
these pirates are usually
recognized by their flag

225
00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:25.090
with a skull and
crossbones on it.

226
00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:29.420
I have my suspicions

227
00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:32.530
that your new friends
fall in line with this kind.

228
00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.740
That's absurd!

229
00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.210
You mean that these
people were criminals

230
00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:37.130
before they set
foot on our shore?

231
00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:40.800
They may not live
by the rules of their world,

232
00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:43.350
but I can't necessarily
call that criminal.

233
00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:45.140
There are those who
fall out of grace

234
00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:47.430
with the rule of law
in any society.

235
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:50.480
I don't see you two as
any different from them.

236
00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:54.520
Whose says that those
who don't fit in are wrong

237
00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:55.940
and others are right?

238
00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:58.580
Sometimes the way of the world
is backwards and blurred

239
00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:01.670
and it can change in an instant.

240
00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:05.460
For example, you kill a man in
war and you're branded a hero.

241
00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:07.240
Kill the same man in peacetime

242
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.370
and you're prosecuted
as a murderer.

243
00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:14.580
I, myself, had a pirate
friend at long time ago.

244
00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:17.810
He came here with his band
more than 20 years ago,

245
00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:20.140
while I was still
God of Skypiea.

246
00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.890
They were funny, all of them.

247
00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:24.060
Boisterous people with
lots to laugh about

248
00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:25.980
and a general air of freedom.

249
00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:28.650
I hated to say goodbye.

250
00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:32.240
The beauty of this land
masks a truth as old as time.

251
00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:35.120
Skypiea is entangled
in endless war.

252
00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:36.390
We, the people of the sky,

253
00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:39.060
wage this battle with
those we call guerillas.

254
00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:40.580
The Shandorians.

255
00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:43.360
Even now they move
against Eneru constantly,

256
00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.290
trying to siege the sky.

257
00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.210
I worry for all those
I could not protect.

258
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.120
When you were God, you did
all that you could to coexist.

259
00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:54.700
Even the Shandorians
were convinced of this.

260
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:55.970
You gave all of us hope

261
00:16:56.050 --> 00:16:58.430
that the several-hundred-year
war would end

262
00:16:58.480 --> 00:17:01.110
and leave us with lasting peace.

263
00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:04.660
I didn't
have near enough time.

264
00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:08.700
Eneru dethroned me before I
could solidify the treaty.

265
00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:10.250
Wasted efforts.

266
00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.930
I'm sorry for failing my people.

267
00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:14.100
Stop that.

268
00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:16.560
You have nothing
to apologize for.

269
00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:21.550
A legend is passed
down through the generations

270
00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:24.110
in Skypiea about its beginnings.

271
00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.840
It is said that
the day the Upper Yard,

272
00:17:28.930 --> 00:17:31.140
the sacred grounds, was created,

273
00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:33.900
the voice of the island sung
forth a beautiful song

274
00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.320
that echoed through the skies.

275
00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.570
It was after that moment
that the tragedy

276
00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:42.540
between the people of the sky
and the Shandorians began...

277
00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.660
As if on cue.

278
00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.390
And so the legend says,

279
00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.710
when we next hear the
singing voice of the island,

280
00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:53.660
this war will finally
come to an end.

281
00:17:54.660 --> 00:17:57.080
The... voice...

282
00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:59.080
That's right.

283
00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:02.390
And our sacred land
will sing again someday.

284
00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:06.020
Someday she must.

285
00:18:17.180 --> 00:18:19.260
Huh? Is something happening?

286
00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:21.770
Nothing you need worry about.

287
00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:23.270
I've got a job to do.

288
00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:24.900
You'll be safe here.

289
00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:37.810
Suu?

290
00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.920
He's right.

291
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.880
This pumpkin juice is fantastic.

292
00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:06.760
Yes. He's quite good
at cultivating things.

293
00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:08.970
Suu, suu!

294
00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:24.930
Just stop
burning the ship!

295
00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.430
I'm serious, I don't wanna die!

296
00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:31.640
Heh.

297
00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:33.310
This is gonna hurt!

298
00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:06.950
Oh, no. Oh, no!

299
00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:08.610
If you want me, that's fine!

300
00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:10.160
But you can't have the ship!

301
00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:12.830
They put me in charge of it,
and I'm not letting them down,

302
00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:17.120
so you back off now,
mister!

303
00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.420
What do you think
we should do, Fuza?

304
00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:22.560
\He's so impassioned.

305
00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:25.080
<b>Fuza Nine-Meter Bird</b>

306
00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:27.670
He doesn't want us
to hurt any of his friends,

307
00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:29.940
he's begging us not
to torch his ship,

308
00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.210
and he says, of course,
that he doesn't want to die.

309
00:20:34.150 --> 00:20:35.610
\I'm at a loss here.

310
00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:40.970
<b>"Sky Rider" Shura Skypiea Priest</b>

311
00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:38.700
\You're a greedy
little hairball, aren't you?

312
00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:41.030
\And you get under my skin.

313
00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:52.770
It's Gan Fall.

314
00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.400
...why don't you try
putting up a fight?!

315
00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.480
Your spear!

316
00:21:00.560 --> 00:21:02.520
It's burning through the metal!

317
00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.620
Hot! Hot!

318
00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.580
Why's he burning
everything?!

319
00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:15.290
You creep!

320
00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.090
Are you trying
to survive this...

321
00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:25.070
...without sacrificing
anything of yourself?

322
00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.070
There's more to
this guy than he's showing me.

323
00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:28.610
He's not just a fighter.

324
00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:31.110
It's like he can predict
all of my moves!

325
00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.480
For one to live,
another must die.

326
00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.860
That is the way of the world.

327
00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.820
This is a sacrificial altar.

328
00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:45.390
What did you
think was going to happen

329
00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:47.900
by you being up here?

330
00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.230
I was supposed to fix the ship

331
00:21:49.310 --> 00:21:51.820
and wait until my
crewmates came back.

332
00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:54.190
Be assured, your friends
are trying their hardest

333
00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:55.740
to get back here.

334
00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:59.300
Of course, they're going to
find it incredibly difficult.

335
00:21:59.390 --> 00:22:01.930
On this island
there are four areas,

336
00:22:01.990 --> 00:22:05.910
\each of which is governed
by a different priest.

337
00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:10.640
<b>Iron Balls</b>
<b>String</b>
<b>Swamp</b>

338
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:09.130
\Our first rule is that when
the targets are in one area,

339
00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:11.750
\the other priests are not
supposed to interfere with them

340
00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:20.150
<b>Iron Balls</b>
<b>String</b>
<b>Swamp</b>

341
00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:13.710
\in any way.

342
00:22:13.790 --> 00:22:15.960
\But this sacrificial altar

343
00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.150
<b>Sacrificial Altar</b>

344
00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:19.380
\doesn't sit inside the
perimeter of any of the areas.

345
00:22:19.450 --> 00:22:21.990
\Here, we are in a free zone.

346
00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:26.040
Which means that any one of us
can attack those we find here.

347
00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:29.190
And proper etiquette would not
have those at the altar killed

348
00:22:29.270 --> 00:22:33.060
until after the targets fail
at a challenge and die.

349
00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:36.630
What?! Luffy and the
others are dead?!

350
00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:38.060
Calm yourself.

351
00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:40.690
The fact that I am here
does not necessarily mean

352
00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:42.910
your friends are
dead at this point.

353
00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:45.150
It's unfortunate but true.

354
00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:46.580
I stand before you now

355
00:22:46.650 --> 00:22:49.240
with a different purpose
than sacrifice.

356
00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:51.470
What's different about it?

357
00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:54.530
Wait. You mean if my friends
get back here and rescue me,

358
00:22:54.630 --> 00:22:55.710
then we're free to go.

359
00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:57.920
But you won't let
that happen, will you?

360
00:22:58.010 --> 00:23:00.680
Well, that depends on you

361
00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:02.810
and whether you and your
crew can make your escape

362
00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:04.770
from the free zone fast enough.

363
00:23:04.910 --> 00:23:05.740
What?

364
00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:07.940
But hold that thought.

365
00:23:08.050 --> 00:23:10.970
The reason I'm here is because
those are the judgment rules

366
00:23:11.060 --> 00:23:12.930
under normal conditions.

367
00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:16.020
However, when there is
an exceptional situation,

368
00:23:16.080 --> 00:23:18.240
the rules are set
to change a little.

369
00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:19.460
Exceptional?

370
00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:22.480
Yes. Exceptional.

371
00:23:22.570 --> 00:23:23.910
Say, for example,

372
00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:26.120
three sacrifices were
to escape the altar

373
00:23:26.200 --> 00:23:28.660
and swing to the main
island using vines.

374
00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:32.120
Oh, that kind of situation.

375
00:23:32.210 --> 00:23:33.630
I say we should cross over

376
00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:36.420
and see what's on the
other side of the river.

377
00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:47.740
are your fault.

378
00:23:47.830 --> 00:23:49.580
You're losin' it.

379
00:23:49.660 --> 00:23:51.410
Someone has to lose their life

380
00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:54.960
to bring balance back
after your friends' escape.

381
00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:56.380
It's atonement.

382
00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:58.800
And sacrifice is part of life.

383
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.300
I want them to see it
when they come back...

384
00:24:01.370 --> 00:24:05.580
their good friend lying on deck,
the life drained from him.

385
00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:09.810
Then they will realize the
severity of their mistakes.

386
00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:13.270
And now...

387
00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:15.800
...I offer your life to God!

388
00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.300
No!

389
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:29.160
Now die.

390
00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:45.050
Sorry to keep you waiting.

391
00:24:45.460 --> 00:24:47.970
It's Gan Fall the Sky Knight!

392
00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:55.250
I wasn't
expecting company.

393
00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:03.230
Gan Fal!l

394
00:25:06.490 --> 00:25:10.750
I knew you wouldn't
let me down, Sky Knight!

395
00:25:10.820 --> 00:25:13.160
We're not dealing
with an amateur here, Pierre.

396
00:25:13.240 --> 00:25:15.370
I wouldn't want to disappoint
a worthy opponent

397
00:25:15.450 --> 00:25:16.830
with anything but our best.

398
00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:21.920
What could that decrepit old
relic possibly be doing here?

399
00:25:22.210 --> 00:25:24.750
Do you feel like putting
him in his place?

400
00:25:26.630 --> 00:25:28.050
Enough stalling!

401
00:25:28.170 --> 00:25:31.130
We don't need
two Gods on this island!

402
00:25:38.430 --> 00:25:42.230
Go, Sky Knight!

403
00:26:24.380 --> 00:26:28.210
Sky Knight, you're my hero!

404
00:26:40.310 --> 00:26:41.850
One more hit in the right spot

405
00:26:41.940 --> 00:26:43.980
should do it for
him, eh, Pierre?

406
00:26:50.700 --> 00:26:51.780
I've had enough.

407
00:26:53.950 --> 00:26:57.330
You're nothing but a pathetic
shell of your former self.

408
00:26:57.410 --> 00:27:01.000
And I'm through playing
games with a fool.

409
00:27:01.080 --> 00:27:02.830
You showed up to this
fight a criminal,

410
00:27:02.920 --> 00:27:05.130
which leaves me
only one option...

411
00:27:05.210 --> 00:27:06.380
take you out.

412
00:27:06.530 --> 00:27:08.110
Hm?

413
00:27:08.200 --> 00:27:11.160
Ordeal of String!

414
00:27:28.170 --> 00:27:30.930
Aha! You're still alive!

415
00:27:31.010 --> 00:27:32.260
I'm impressed!

416
00:27:32.300 --> 00:27:35.720
And as a reward
for good behavior,

417
00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:37.550
we're going to finish
our little fun today

418
00:27:37.640 --> 00:27:40.260
with a move I've received
several awards for.

419
00:27:45.020 --> 00:27:47.140
Ha, ha, ha!

420
00:27:48.810 --> 00:27:51.440
My super secret surprise!

421
00:27:51.520 --> 00:27:55.780
Sphere Dragon!

422
00:28:05.210 --> 00:28:10.210
<b>Shandian Settlement of Guerrillas</b>
<b>Village Hidden in the Clouds</b>

423
00:28:16.060 --> 00:28:19.400
– Aisa!

424
00:28:19.510 --> 00:28:20.680
Where have you been, child?

425
00:28:21.550 --> 00:28:22.680
Ah! Kamakiri!

426
00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:24.930
The Upper Yard again, right?

427
00:28:25.160 --> 00:28:27.580
And that's probably
Vearth in your bag.

428
00:28:28.890 --> 00:28:31.190
Stay away
from that place, Aisa...

429
00:28:32.650 --> 00:28:34.440
...or you will die.

430
00:28:38.320 --> 00:28:40.200
You can't tell me what to do!

431
00:28:40.780 --> 00:28:43.330
You haven't even been
able to beat Eneru yet!

432
00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:49.370
What a brat.

433
00:28:50.880 --> 00:28:51.970
An opportunity?

434
00:28:52.050 --> 00:28:53.300
That's right.

435
00:28:53.390 --> 00:28:55.260
For some reason, Gan Fall
entered the Upper Yard,

436
00:28:55.350 --> 00:28:57.810
which of course drew the
attention of the priests.

437
00:28:57.890 --> 00:29:00.600
You see, that old bag of bones
thinks it's his responsibility

438
00:29:00.710 --> 00:29:03.290
to protect the
people of Skypiea.

439
00:29:03.380 --> 00:29:05.460
And that will only
make him weak.

440
00:29:08.130 --> 00:29:09.550
We would be wise to strike

441
00:29:09.550 --> 00:29:12.130
while our enemies are
occupied with each other!

442
00:29:15.280 --> 00:29:19.740
<b>Warrior of Shandora Wyper</b>
<b>A Shandian</b>

443
00:29:15.470 --> 00:29:20.270
\The Great Warrior Kalgara said,
"Light the fire of Shandora."

444
00:29:20.350 --> 00:29:22.730
Our people will do just that.

445
00:29:22.810 --> 00:29:24.560
No one can deny us our destiny,

446
00:29:24.630 --> 00:29:28.920
be it Gan Fall and or Eneru, and
now is the time to take action!

447
00:29:29.010 --> 00:29:31.130
They have had the
audacity to reign as "God"

448
00:29:31.220 --> 00:29:32.590
and that is unforgivable.

449
00:29:32.770 --> 00:29:35.020
No matter how different from
one another they may seem,

450
00:29:35.110 --> 00:29:36.720
I assure you they are the same.

451
00:29:36.720 --> 00:29:38.840
And they must be eliminated!

452
00:29:40.730 --> 00:29:41.890
Wyper.

453
00:29:41.950 --> 00:29:43.200
Huh?

454
00:29:43.310 --> 00:29:46.350
It has been six years since
Eneru began his reign.

455
00:29:46.410 --> 00:29:48.500
And for the first time
since he took power,

456
00:29:48.560 --> 00:29:50.770
a rebel has appeared
on Angel Island.

457
00:29:50.860 --> 00:29:52.730
A young woman, I hear.

458
00:29:52.840 --> 00:29:54.750
Get to the point, Laki.

459
00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:58.050
Because the Sky Knight rescued
the young rebel from judgment,

460
00:29:58.130 --> 00:30:01.050
Eneru now has reason to
directly confront Gan Fall

461
00:30:01.140 --> 00:30:03.100
in order to judge him.

462
00:30:03.160 --> 00:30:05.580
A battle like this between the
former God and the current God

463
00:30:05.660 --> 00:30:07.040
has never happened.

464
00:30:07.120 --> 00:30:10.340
Strategically, this could be
most advantageous to us.

465
00:30:12.030 --> 00:30:15.780
We must remember that Gan Fall
has never harmed any of us.

466
00:30:15.870 --> 00:30:17.700
Not as the Sky Knight,

467
00:30:17.790 --> 00:30:20.790
and not during his reign as God.

468
00:30:20.870 --> 00:30:23.290
The fact that he never hurt
any of us doesn't change that

469
00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:25.990
he ruled with absolute
authority as "God."

470
00:30:26.090 --> 00:30:28.180
And although he is
our enemy's enemy,

471
00:30:28.270 --> 00:30:30.400
that does not make him our ally.

472
00:30:30.480 --> 00:30:32.690
If he and one of the priests
kill each other in battle,

473
00:30:32.770 --> 00:30:35.280
that will serve our
purposes just fine.

474
00:30:35.360 --> 00:30:37.860
Otherwise he is of no use to us.

475
00:30:40.320 --> 00:30:42.660
If you have any doubts
at all about this fight,

476
00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:44.620
stay out!

477
00:30:44.680 --> 00:30:46.520
You'll just be in the way!

478
00:30:50.040 --> 00:30:51.040
Hm?

479
00:30:51.070 --> 00:30:53.280
– Aisa!

480
00:30:53.370 --> 00:30:54.620
Upper Yard? What Upper Yard?

481
00:30:54.700 --> 00:30:57.790
I didn't go to Upper Yard,
I promise you I didn't!

482
00:30:57.790 --> 00:31:00.460
You can't go into the tent yet.

483
00:31:02.080 --> 00:31:04.540
Wyper, descendent of the
Great Warrior Kalgara,

484
00:31:04.680 --> 00:31:06.350
is angry right now.

485
00:31:06.410 --> 00:31:07.540
Careful.

486
00:31:09.540 --> 00:31:12.790
Oh. He's scary when he gets mad.

487
00:31:14.770 --> 00:31:16.400
Scarier than God.

488
00:31:20.590 --> 00:31:26.050
Help them? Us? How?

489
00:31:26.140 --> 00:31:28.640
Conis. My dear child.

490
00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:30.850
It's only right that
you and I should try

491
00:31:30.930 --> 00:31:33.440
to create some way
for them to escape.

492
00:31:45.220 --> 00:31:47.680
Wow, I can't believe
how fast they are.

493
00:31:49.290 --> 00:31:50.460
Awesome.

494
00:31:51.460 --> 00:31:54.130
I can see that diplomacy is

495
00:31:54.210 --> 00:31:57.090
no longer an option for me.

496
00:31:57.170 --> 00:31:59.970
Diplomacy
is for the weak!

497
00:32:03.220 --> 00:32:05.570
This battle is intense.

498
00:32:12.410 --> 00:32:14.250
Heaven's judgment.

499
00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.410
That young woman
did something foolish.

500
00:32:20.330 --> 00:32:22.710
She brought this upon us.

501
00:32:22.780 --> 00:32:25.240
She knows we're not
supposed to anger him!

502
00:32:45.090 --> 00:32:47.380
Please come back to us...

503
00:32:47.510 --> 00:32:48.770
...God.

504
00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:57.980
You're mine!

505
00:33:03.590 --> 00:33:06.130
Is something wrong, Gan Fall?

506
00:33:06.400 --> 00:33:09.160
Shura! What've you done?

507
00:33:09.290 --> 00:33:11.250
Why can't we move?

508
00:33:12.250 --> 00:33:13.710
You old fool.

509
00:33:15.050 --> 00:33:16.800
Time to die!

510
00:33:29.680 --> 00:33:32.850
Mysterious... the strings are.

511
00:33:34.610 --> 00:33:37.780
If you have the
audacity to enter Upper Yard,

512
00:33:37.860 --> 00:33:40.570
you must answer to
the four priests.

513
00:33:40.660 --> 00:33:44.250
You were foolish...
to think you could beat us.

514
00:33:44.320 --> 00:33:47.150
He's falling! Oh, no!

515
00:33:48.910 --> 00:33:51.830
God Eneru is glorious,

516
00:33:51.910 --> 00:33:55.200
perfect, and far
beyond your reach.

517
00:34:01.440 --> 00:34:04.560
And our sacred land
will sing again someday.

518
00:34:04.560 --> 00:34:05.900
Someday she must.

519
00:34:07.130 --> 00:34:09.880
Sky Knight! Sky Knight!
